  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "extra_component",
      "components": ["J4"],
      "pins": ["J4.1", "J4.2"],
      "nets": ["GND", "/Microcontroller/NET0008"],
      "observed": "The netlist places a 2-pin screw terminal, J4, between the heater control net /Microcontroller/NET0008 and GND. That same net is connected to ESP32 GPIO1, the TPS1H200AQDGNRQ1 IN and DIAG_EN pins, and the status LED D3/R2 path.",
      "expected": "The specification describes the heater control path as being driven only by ESP32 GPIO1 to the high-side switch inputs, with a status LED/resistor on that net. It does not describe an external screw terminal that can short the control signal to ground.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"6\") (name \"/Microcontroller/NET0008\") ... (node (ref \"J4\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"Pin_2\") (pintype \"passive\")) ... (node (ref \"U4\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"IN\") (pintype \"input\")) ... (node (ref \"U4\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"DIAG_EN\") (pintype \"input\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"8\") (name \"GND\") ... (node (ref \"J4\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"Pin_1\") (pintype \"passive\")) ...)"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "IN/DIAG_EN (pins 1/2) are both driven from ESP32 GPIO1 (net /Microcontroller/HEATER)"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "If a wire, jumper, or connector is placed across J4, GPIO1 and the high-side switch input are pulled to ground. This would prevent the heater from turning on and, when GPIO1 is driven high, create a direct output-to-ground contention that could stress or damage the MCU pin. The intended design has no such external shorting path on the heater control line.",
      "confidence": 0.55
    }
  ],
  "summary": "Most connectivity and component values match the specification, but the netlist contains an unmentioned screw terminal J4 tying the heater control net to ground, which deviates from the intended MCU-only heater control path."
}

